{
  "bridge_text": "The secret of Mosk's grumpiness remains tucked away in the shadows for now, but the stairs beckon us deeper into the tree. Let us see what happens when Lina tries to win over the grumpy fox.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Lina stood firm, her eyes bright with curiosity despite his stern warning. She knew that a heart as prickly as his must be hiding something precious, and she was not about to leave until she understood why."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed a shaky claw at the door, but Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set it on the step between them, offering it as a peace token for the trouble of walking her down. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his grey fur bristling. Then he stood up, tucked his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With grumpy Mosk blocking the way, Lina stood her ground. Since she could not leave without hearing the song, she decided to try a different approach.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed sternly at the exit, his tail flicking with annoyance. Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set the fruit on the step between them and whispered that it was a gift for his trouble. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his sharp eyes softening. Finally, he stood up, straightened his patched vest, and stepped onto the first stair to lead the way."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Deep at the bottom of the stairs, the humming revealed itself as a quiet, rhythmic song. A firefly the size of a robin lay curled on a bed of moss, her golden glow fading to a dim flicker. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked at her. He confessed that she had been his dearest friend, but long ago he had failed to bring her medicine. Now, he guarded the tree in silence, too ashamed to face the light he had let go out."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
